# support: a sacrificial support at the bench (decision C16), as a 3D
# printer's slicer adds supports and they are cut away after. A ceramic
# disc (C1) in the vise; the wire feeder feeds 30 mm of steel wire, a
# support; the arm takes it and the feeder cuts it; the arm brings its
# end to the disc's lead 1, pincer P1 grips the support, the arm goes;
# the welder station welds the support's tab to the lead. The vise
# opens: the disc is held by the support alone, and the turntable turns
# and tilts it. The vise closes on it again; the cutter station cuts the
# tab free, P1 lets the support go, and it falls into the bin.
reset circuit=weld
tool A tweezers
pick A C1 grasp=body
place A C1 at=0,0,-20
vise close
release A C1
lift A mm=60
wire S5 awg=22 mm=30 metal=steel support=yes
pick A W1 grasp=middle
cut S5
lift A mm=60
move A to=0,60,60 rpy=180,0,45
move A to=-28.147,10.607,-27.746
align A W1.1.tip to=C1.1.6 gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=W1.2 at=8
release A W1
lift A mm=60
present C1.1+W1.1 at=S3
scope aim=C1.1+W1.1 zoom=8
weld S3 at=C1.1+W1.1 energy=8
vise open
stage turn=60 tilt=-20
stage turn=-60 tilt=0
vise close
inspect supports
present W1.1.12 at=S4
scope aim=W1.1 zoom=4
trim S4 on=W1.1 at=12
unpinch P1
inspect supports
